-- title:
--   Divisibility of the toric point subgroups
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and suppose $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. the image of $p$ lies in `A.nonunits`. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $N_0$, $p$ and $A$ — a morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to `base p` compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ with structure morphism $f$ to `base p`, a relative group law on $f$ over `baseRing p`, and bijections of $J_0(N_0)$ and of its analogue over the residue field of $A$ with the sections of $f$ over the generic, respectively residual, point — and let $h\Lambda$ assert `Λ.IsJacobian`: the abelian-scheme property bundle for $f$, commutativity of the group law, additivity and Galois equivariance of the two point identifications, agreement of reduction of points when the mod-$\ell$ reduction inputs hold, and realisation of each element of the Hecke algebra by an endomorphism of $f$ compatible with the group law. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, and let $m, d > 0$. Then for every $y$ in the subgroup $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ of $J_0(N_0 p)$ — the subgroup generated by the range of the family $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ — there exists $z \in \mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}\,(m d)$ with $d \cdot z = y$.
--
--   This expresses the divisibility of the tower of toric torsion subgroups of the level-$N_0p$ Néron object: the toric points of level $m$ are $d$-fold multiples of toric points of level $md$, reflecting the compatibility of the toric lifts along $\mu_m^t \hookrightarrow \mu_{md}^t$. It is one of the elementary inputs to the comparison of the toric torsion with the toric monodromy part, used by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.toricPts_le_toricMonodromyPart_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.toricPts_le_toricMonodromyPart_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts).
